menu "My UPS Pal setup access point"

config UPSA_AP_WINDOW_S
    int "Seconds the setup AP stays up with nobody on it (0: for ever)"
    default 0
    range 0 86400
    help
        0 is the upstream behaviour and the default: the setup access point
        stays up until the board joins a network. Right when the board is
        useless until it does.

        Set it, and a board that has not joined a network keeps its access
        point for this long and then turns the radio OFF -- not a hidden
        SSID, off. The clock restarts whenever a client is associated, so it
        never closes under someone's feet while they are configuring it, and
        it restarts again on every press of BOOT.

        For this adapter the UPS data goes out over RS485 and the radio exists
        only so a technician can open the page. Leaving an open access point
        broadcasting for years in twenty customer buildings is a standing
        invitation; ten minutes after power-up is enough to configure a board.

        THE WAY BACK IS PHYSICAL, by design: press BOOT, or power-cycle the
        board, and the window starts again. Both are available to anyone who
        can reach the board, and neither needs the network that is off.

        A board that HAS joined a network is never touched by this: its radio
        is carrying data.

endmenu
